-**Pitfalls:**
-*   **Discreteness Artifacts:** The precalculated weights have limited resolution (6 bits). This can cause visible artifacts, though 6 bits is considered sufficient to make them invisible to the viewer [S1].
-*   **Boundary Handling:** The controller returns 0 for out-of-bounds addresses, which must be handled correctly to avoid incorrect gradient calculations at volume edges [S1].
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** Addresses outside the data cube return 0. This must be handled by the memory controller to prevent out-of-bounds errors [S1].
+*   **Quantization Artifacts:** The discreteness of the pre-calculated weights (6-bit resolution) can cause visible artifacts. The 6-bit resolution is chosen specifically to make these artifacts invisible to the viewer [S1].
+*   **Memory Bandwidth:** High data rates (640 MB/s) require careful memory bank management (Fast Page Mode, alternate read-out) to avoid conflicts when accessing 8 neighbors simultaneously [S1].
 
